1
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Tony Manero knows the old days are over. But nobody's
gonna tell him he can't feel that good again.

2
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Staying Alive is a drama, music film directed by Sylvester Stallone.

3
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
It's five years later and Tony Manero's Saturday Night Fever is still burning.

4
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Now he's strutting toward his biggest challenger yet -
making it as a dancer on the Broadway stage.

5
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Tony Manero, played by John Travolta.

6
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Jackie, played by Cynthia Rhodes.

7
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Laura, played by Finola Hughes.

8
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Jesse, played by Steve Inwood.

9
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Mrs. Manero, played by Julie Bovasso.

10
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Butler, played by Charles Ward.

11
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Staying Alive is a 1983 American dance drama film and the
sequel to Saturday Night Fever (1977).

12
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
It was directed by Sylvester Stallone, produced by Stallone and the Saturday Night
Fever producer Robert Stigwood, and written by Stallone and Norman Wexler.

13
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
It stars John Travolta, reprising his Saturday Night Fever role as Tony Manero, with Cynthia
Rhodes, Finola Hughes, Joyce Hyser, Julie Bovasso, Viktor Manoel and Kevyn Morrow.

14
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The title comes from the Bee Gees song of the same name, which was used as the theme song to
Saturday Night Fever and is played during the final scene of Staying Alive.

15
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Theatrically released on July 15, 1983, Staying Alive received negative reviews.

16
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
It earned $127 million worldwide on a $22 million budget.

17
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
It featured the song "Far from Over" by Stallone's brother Frank Stallone,
which reached #10 on the Billboard Hot 100 and the Cashbox charts.

18
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
The film explores themes of career, dancing master, nightclub, disco, broadway.

19
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
The tone is emotional.
